---
source: bin/tests/shell_idiom.rs
---
stdenv.mkDerivation { installPhase = ''
  runHook "preInstall"
  cp ${src} dst; chown ${owner} dst; chmod 755 dst
  cp src existingDir; chmod 700 existingDir
  cat Cargo.toml | read value
  rm -f dst && ln -s src dst
  runHook "postInstall"
''; }
---
[shellcheck] Advice: ShellCheck found issues in an inline shell script
   ╭─[ <temp_file_path>:5:20 ]
   │
 5 │   cat Cargo.toml | read value
   │                    ──┬─  
   │                      ╰─── SC2162: read without -r will mangle backslashes.
───╯
[shell_idiom] Advice: Shell commands with a shorter idiom
   ╭─[ <temp_file_path>:3:3 ]
   │
 3 │   cp ${src} dst; chown ${owner} dst; chmod 755 dst
   │   ────────────────────────┬───────────────────────  
   │                           ╰───────────────────────── cp + chown + chmod can be one install
 4 │   cp src existingDir; chmod 700 existingDir
   │   ────────────────────┬────────────────────  
   │                       ╰────────────────────── cp + chmod can be one install
 5 │   cat Cargo.toml | read value
   │   ─────────────┬─────────────  
   │                ╰─────────────── cat only feeds read: read the file directly
 6 │   rm -f dst && ln -s src dst
   │   ─────────────┬────────────  
   │                ╰────────────── rm -f then ln -s: ln -sfn replaces the link
───╯
